{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unavailable job log can repeatedly prevent later PR changes from being recorded."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A valid repository capitalization mismatch leaves CI classification pending and can block observation of later PRs."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Failures paused because main is red can disappear from the historical ledger when the PR advances."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A later sibling-only rerun can leave the originating rerun unresolved and block later PR observations."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A completed skipped or neutral rerun remains pending indefinitely, leaving the PR stuck."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A main-branch failure reported as a legacy status can be missed, causing an unnecessary PR rerun instead of a pause."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The demonstrated behavior permits a rerun that may also execute a security job, but the evidence does not establish a prohibited ledger or quarantine action."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A test-owned timeout in a supported-looking format is treated as a failure needing a fix instead of receiving the intended retry."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A definitively rejected rerun remains claimed indefinitely, leaving the PR waiting without an actionable result."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"A long setup preamble can displace failure context from the feed excerpt even though the separate signature identifies the failure."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A misleading matching line can collide across distinct failures, suppressing a ledger entry and an automatic retry."},{"id":"C14","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Repeated inspections of unchanged paused PRs can exhaust the shared REST allowance and delay observation."},{"id":"C11b","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"A long setup preamble can cause the excerpt to omit later failure context."},{"id":"C12b","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The extra additive migration applies successfully and represents optional cleanup without a demonstrated runtime effect."},{"id":"C7b","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Rerunning a job can repeat a passing security step, but the evidence does not establish that this violates the stated ledger and quarantine exclusion."}]}